Port B as the gate

http://b/{sys}/…

• b/index.php — lists every folder that has an index.php as a surface system
• b/.htaccess — all paths rewrite into that SYS’s index.php (URI preserved for keyMaker)
• One host, many surfaces — no new vhost per room

Live under b/: terminal, starline, www, mailroom, mythleak, nim, backrooms, book, interra — each the same two papers:

┌─────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ File                │ Job                                                                        │
├─────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ -SKY_SIG-{sys}.php  │ Who am I? SYS_ID, display tags, $GLOBALS[SITE]…                            │
├─────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ -SKY_AUTH-{sys}.php │ Boot chain: routes → SIG → invokeSky → env → local config c/{sys}/--SIG--… │
├─────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ index.php           │ Enter ritual: AUTH → keyMaker() → lockAndKey() → getSkyAUTH(shell)         │
└─────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

The enter ritual (every surface)

require_once __DIR__ . '/-SKY_AUTH-{sys}.php';
keyMaker();
lockAndKey();
getSkyAUTH(ROUTE_TO_SHELL);

1. keyMaker() (getROOMKEY.skyLINE.php)
Parse path into room + key:

/{SYS}/{DOM}/{KEY}     unified port b
/{DOM}/{KEY}           dedicated vhost

Strips the SYS segment when present → $_GET[DOM] = KEY.

2. lockAndKey()
• Reads allowed doors from $GLOBALS[SITE]['tDOM'] (from c/{sys}/-FIG--nav.php)
• Room must be a known DOM
• Key file must exist:
  m/doors/{SYS}/{DOM}/{KEY}.php
• Missing room → No Room Found
• Room without key → Room Without Key
• Bad key → No Key Found
• Hit → require that room file, then shell

3. Room file (e.g. m/doors/terminal/io/login.php)
Calls SKY__AUTH(mod, display, dom, …, room, …) then draws the room (tools, sky, etc.).

4. Terminal network example of multi-“surface” inside one SYS

c/terminal/-FIG--nav.php:

tDOM = base, io, ab, icu, rx   // future: jx, cu…

Rooms on disk:

m/doors/terminal/
  base/login.php
  io/login.php, files.php, import.php, …
  ab/…  icu/…  rx/…

So enter/leave = change path → new DOM/KEY → auth against tDOM → load room paper → shell. Not “one app.js tab.”

Layers (map to PORT-EDN / XOS)

┌───────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┐
│ myPI B-chain              │ Meaning                       │ EDN-ish name (your place doc) │
├───────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤
│ SYS (b/terminal)          │ Surface system / destination  │ surface / destination         │
├───────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤
│ DOM (io, ab)              │ District / station face       │ district or place segment     │
├───────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤
│ KEY / ROOM (files, login) │ Room inside that face         │ room                          │
├───────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤
│ SIG                       │ Identity of the system        │ surface.cfg identity          │
├───────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤
│ AUTH chain                │ Boot + package routes         │ hollow core boot              │
├───────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤
│ tDOM                      │ Allow-list of doors           │ surface/room registry         │
├───────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤
│ m/doors/…                 │ Actual room implementations   │ room packages / configs       │
├───────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┤
│ shell (a/{sys}/)          │ Render vessel after key works │ surface shell dressup         │
└───────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┘

PLACE-AND-NAMING already says: drop domination vocabulary in new language; path is what matters.